0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Vera Therapeutics, Inc., a clinical stage biotechnology company, focuses on the development and commercialization of transformative treatments for patients with immunological diseases. The company offers atacicept, a fully humanized TACI-Fc fusion protein that binds B-cell activating factor (BAFF) and A proliferation-inducing ligand (APRIL), which is self-administered at home as a subcutaneous injection being evaluated for the treatment of immunoglobulin A nephropathy (IgAN) and other autoimmune kidney diseases. It is also developing MAU868, a human monoclonal antibody for the treatment of BK viremia infections that has completed phase 2 clinical trial; and VT-109, a novel BAFF/APRIL dual-inhibitor B cell maturation antigen (BCMA) molecule to treat B cell mediated autoimmune diseases. The company was formerly known as Trucode Gene Repair, Inc. and changed its name to Vera Therapeutics, Inc. in April 2020. Vera Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Marshall W. Fordyce M.D. | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 362 people. Stock-based compensation of $105K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Vera Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.5B market cap.","The company is burning through $242M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -41.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.17) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 132% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Vera Therapeutics Stock Surged Today (Hint: It's Not Great News For Vertex Shareholders)","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/heres-why-vera-therapeutics-stock-182713000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795804159.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Z